{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>The words of a whisperer</b> — also [verses 8 and 26 in chapters 8–9?]. Two adjacent verses. <b>Like wounds</b> [כמתלהמים]: like things hidden and covered, like the words of a whisperer that he speaks in secret. <b>And the belly</b> [ובטן]: like 'the heart,' and also to include, meaning: the matter of a sluggard — he too goes slack in his work, so that he does not do it when he is a whisperer."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The bracketed [ח-ט] is obscure; it may be a chapter/verse range marker or a textual corruption, and its referent is uncertain. The word כמתלהמים is Ibn Ezra's reading/interpretation of the Hebrew; translated hyper-literally. The final sentence connecting the sluggard to the whisperer is textually difficult and rendered as literally as possible."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:29.821832380Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}